 "extended": "**January 30, 2018**\n\n*KNOT HOMOLOGY AND SHEAVES ON THE HILBERT SCHEME OF POINTS ON*\n\n83 pp, 69 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** For each braid β ∈ Brn we construct a 2-periodic complex Sβ of quasi-coherent C∗ × C∗ - equivariant sheaves on the non-commutative nested Hilbert scheme Hilb f ree 1,n . W e show that the triply graded vector space of the hypercohomology H(Sβ ⊗ ∧ • (B)) with B being tautological vector bundle, is an isotopy invariant of the knot obtained by the closure of β . W e also show that the support of cohomology of the complex Sβ is supported on the ordinary nested Hilbert scheme Hilb 1,n ⊂ Hilbf ree 1,n , that allows us to relate the triply graded knot homology to the sheaves on Hilb 1,n\n\n**Outline.** 1 Introduction; 1.1 Motivation; 1.2 Main result; 1.3 Sheaves on Hilbert schemes; 1.4 Braids and matrix factorizations; 1.5 Structure of the paper; 2 Basic space and Matrix factorizations; 2.1 Notations, conventions; 2.2 Matrix factorizations: three lemmas; 2.3 Koszul matrix factorizations; 3 Equivariant structure of matrix factorizatio; 3.2 Push forward; 3.3 Chevalley-Eilenberg complex; 3.4 Equivariant matrix factorizations; 3.5 Extension lemmas; 3.6 Lifting lemma for morphisms; 3.7 Equivariant push-forward; 4 Convolution algebra: definition\n\n**Extracted claims (proposals, not verified).**\n- Theorem 1.1: For any β∈ Brn the triply graded space:\n- Theorem 1.2: The bi-graded Euler characteristic of Hk(β) is equal to the HOMFLY-PT polynomial of the\n- Theorem 1.3: There is a spectral sequence with E2 term being\n- Theorem 1.6: [34] For any k∈ Z we have\n- Theorem 1.7: The homotopic category MFsc\n- Theorem 9.6: Inside convolution algebra (MFsc",
